# Maps+ Project Rules

Project operating rules, build conventions, key dependencies, and release
workflow for this Splunk custom visualization app live in `CLAUDE.md` at the
repository root.

**Agents: read @CLAUDE.md before performing any build, deploy, or release
task.** Critical items that are easy to miss otherwise:

- `npm install --ignore-scripts` is mandatory inside the viz dir (a
  `node-sass` transitive dep in the `leaflet-measure` fork fails to build on
  modern Node otherwise)
- The compiled `visualization.js` bundle is committed to the repo and MUST
  be rebuilt after every change to `src/maps-plus.js`
- Build and deploy commands run from `appserver/static/visualizations/maps-plus`, not the repo root
- The Splunk app ID is `leaflet_maps_app` (not `maps-plus`)
- Release checklist (version bump → changelog → develop → master merge →
  tag → package verification → GitHub issue triage → Splunkbase notes) is
  pinned in `CLAUDE.md`; do not skip steps

## Planning artifacts

This project uses the GSD (Get Shit Done) workflow for milestone, phase, and
plan tracking. Planning lives in `.planning/`:

- `.planning/STATE.md` — current phase/plan/milestone cursor
- `.planning/ROADMAP.md` — phases under each milestone
- `.planning/REQUIREMENTS.md` — requirement IDs with traceability
- `.planning/phases/NN-slug/` — per-phase artifacts (CONTEXT, RESEARCH, PLAN, UAT, SUMMARY)

GSD subagents (researcher, planner, executor, checker) read these during
phase operations. Keep doc references in `CLAUDE.md` consistent with the
canonical sources above when they overlap.

## When `CLAUDE.md` and this file disagree

`CLAUDE.md` is the source of truth for build/deploy/release detail. This
file is a pointer to ensure both Cursor's rule loader and GSD subagents
find the project operating rules.
